# Frontend UI engineering

Adapted from https://github.com/addyosmani/agent-skills (frontend-ui-engineering); see the
upstream skill for depth.

- **Accessibility:** semantic HTML, labelled controls, keyboard nav, sufficient contrast,
  visible focus. Charts need text/table alternatives or aria summaries for key numbers.
- **States first:** design loading (skeletons), empty (market closed / no data), and error
  (toast + retry) before the happy path. Never an infinite spinner.
- **Performance:** server components by default; lazy-load heavy chart libs on the client;
  memoize expensive renders; virtualize long option-chain tables; avoid layout shift.
- **Consistency:** compose shadcn/ui primitives; one design token set (spacing/color/typography);
  don't hand-roll components that shadcn already provides.
- **Data discipline:** fetch via TanStack Query with sensible cache keys; show stale-while-revalidate;
  never recompute metrics client-side — render what the API returns.
- **Responsiveness:** laptop-first, tablet-tolerable; test at narrow widths.
